"اشحذها الآن" (Sharpen now) rebuilds the signature for the tab you''re on, from that language''s posts only. And if your posting mix changes enough that your primary voice switches, Aura tells you on the card — never silently.', NULL, '{voice,presence,capture}', '{guide,faq}', '55', '2026-06-03 15:11:16.508278+00', '2026-06-05 08:20:34.682198+00') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
Where it lives: in your own private space. Another Aura user can never see it — every record is locked to your account at the database level. That''s enforced, not promised ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
What the team — including the founder — can and can''t see: there''s no screen, report, or button anywhere in Aura that shows us your captures, drafts, or content. We see only aggregate signals and your account status, never the substance of what you read, write, or save. To be straight: as the people who run the service we have database access, like the operators of any tool you use — the difference is that Aura is built with no path that puts your content in front of us, and we don''t go looking ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
What powers Aura: a small set of established providers (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, and Perplexity for intelligence; Supabase for storage; Resend for email). They process your data under business terms that, by default, don''t use it to train their models. The full list is in our Privacy Policy ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
One honest limit: Aura is not end-to-end encrypted, and we won''t pretend it is. For Aura to turn your reading into signals and posts, the system has to read your content. So instead of making it unreadable to the system — which would break the product — we protect it with strict per-account isolation and by having no feature that exposes it ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
